// FIXED 2026-09-08 (dead-op audit): this was declared on cavewalltunnel_to_temple_open, which is the
// state-1 child of the multi-loc cavewalltunnel_to_temple (quest_mourning2/configs/mourning2.loc).
// OpLocHandler resolves the multi only to validate the op and then calls setInteraction with the
// original loc, so a handler on the child never fires - the same trap that killed the Recruitment
// Drive statue handlers. Moved to the shell. State 0 is a solid cave wall with no ops, so this can
// only be reached in state 1, when the tunnel is open. The body is still the unbuilt Mourning's End
// Part II stub it always was.
[oploc1,cavewalltunnel_to_temple]
// Mourning's End Part II is built now, and this is its front door.
if (~mt_tunnel = true) {
    return;
}
switch_coord (loc_coord) {
    case default : @unhandled_stairs(loc_coord);
}

